From 0953b0887c2d39bc1a04d5371d82212140989fd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thedivingshellyfish <jellyqda@systemli.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:06:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Editable entry labels above each entry, orientation graphics
 in step 3
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- the label of each entry (e.g. participant ID from the chosen label
  column/row) sits above its box and can be edited directly; changes
  go into the label item, are saved/exported and can be undone without
  jumping to that item. Without a label item the position in the file
  is shown ("Row 5" / "Column E").
- step 3 shows "items as columns / rows" as graphic cards with a tick,
  like step 1
- item header shows a chip with a mini graphic and the item's position
  ("Column E · Items as columns")

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CwaRKVwrR9hvVWRrni6Bok
